---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Proposal: ZERA on Astro vs Framer">
  <div class="min-h-screen bg-[#030201] text-stone-100 selection:bg-amber-500/30">
    <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[radial-gradient(circle_at_50%_0%,rgba(255,136,0,0.1),transparent_50%)] pointer-events-none"></div>
    
    <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-4xl py-24 container-responsive">
      
      <header class="mb-16 border-b border-amber-300/10 pb-10">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-3 rounded-full border border-amber-500/30 bg-amber-500/10 px-4 py-1.5 mb-6">
          <span class="relative flex h-2 w-2">
            <span class="animate-ping absolute inline-flex h-full w-full rounded-full bg-amber-400 opacity-75"></span>
            <span class="relative inline-flex rounded-full h-2 w-2 bg-amber-500"></span>
          </span>
          <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-amber-200">Strategic Technical Analysis</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="font-display font-extrabold text-white tracking-tight mb-6 title-responsive">
          Why custom code is the only path forward for <span class="text-transparent bg-clip-text bg-gradient-to-r from-amber-200 to-amber-500">ZERA Network</span>.
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-stone-400 leading-relaxed">
          A comprehensive evaluation comparing the current "Low-Code" environment (Framer) against the "Code-First" architecture (Astro + React) we just deployed.
        </p>
      </header>

      <main style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 3rem;">
        <!-- Section 1 -->
        <section class="data-module rounded-[2rem] border border-white/10 bg-black/55 backdrop-blur-xl card-responsive">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-6">
            <div class="flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-amber-500/10 border border-amber-500/20 text-amber-400">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-zap"><path d="M4 14a1 1 0 0 1-.78-1.63l9.9-10.2a.5.5 0 0 1 .86.46l-1.92 6.02A1 1 0 0 0 13 10h7a1 1 0 0 1 .78 1.63l-9.9 10.2a.5.5 0 0 1-.86-.46l1.92-6.02A1 1 0 0 0 11 14z"/></svg>
            </div>
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">1. Performance and Technical SEO (Core Web Vitals)</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-4 text-stone-300 leading-relaxed">
            <p><strong class="text-white">Framer:</strong> It is a React-based platform that ships a significant amount of JavaScript to the browser, even for completely static pages. This blocks the Main Thread, increasing the <em class="text-amber-200">Time to Interactive (TTI)</em> and directly penalizing Google metrics (Core Web Vitals). Furthermore, technical SEO control (like custom Schema Markup or dynamic JSON-LD) is strictly limited to what their interface allows.</p>
            <p><strong class="text-white">Astro (The new web):</strong> Astro uses "Islands Architecture" which ships <strong>zero JavaScript by default</strong>. The page loads instantly as pure HTML, and only hydrates with React the specific components that need interactivity. Flawless performance translates directly into better organic ranking on Google, lower bounce rates, and a truly premium user experience.</p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 2 -->
        <section class="data-module rounded-[2rem] border border-white/10 bg-black/55 backdrop-blur-xl card-responsive">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-6">
            <div class="flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-amber-500/10 border border-amber-500/20 text-amber-400">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-key"><path d="m15.5 7.5 2.3 2.3a1 1 0 0 0 1.4 0l2.1-2.1a1 1 0 0 0 0-1.4L19 4"/><path d="m21 2-9.6 9.6"/><circle cx="7.5" cy="15.5" r="5.5"/></svg>
            </div>
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">2. Absolute Ownership (No Vendor Lock-in)</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-4 text-stone-300 leading-relaxed">
            <p><strong class="text-white">Framer:</strong> ZERA is essentially renting its digital presence. If Framer raises prices, changes its policies, or suffers network outages, ZERA is affected without recourse. The most critical flaw: <strong>you cannot export your code</strong>. You are trapped in their proprietary ecosystem.</p>
            <p><strong class="text-white">Astro (The new web):</strong> ZERA owns 100% of the Intellectual Property. Everything resides in your GitHub repository. You can deploy it to any infrastructure in the world (AWS, Cloudflare, Vercel, GitHub Pages) for free or pennies. If the project scales massively, the code scales with you; you own every single line.</p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Section 3 -->
        <section class="data-module rounded-[2rem] border border-white/10 bg-black/55 backdrop-blur-xl card-responsive">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-4 mb-6">
            <div class="flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-amber-500/10 border border-amber-500/20 text-amber-400">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-blocks"><rect width="7" height="7" x="14" y="3" rx="1"/><path d="M10 21V8a1 1 0 0 0-1-1H4a1 1 0 0 0-1 1v12a1 1 0 0 0 1 1h12a1 1 0 0 0 1-1v-5a1 1 0 0 0-1-1H3"/></svg>
            </div>
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white">3. Web3 Integration and Scalability</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="space-y-4 text-stone-300 leading-relaxed">
            <p><strong class="text-white">Framer:</strong> Integrating real Web3 logic (wallet connections like Phantom or MetaMask, reading on-chain smart contracts, staking dashboards, or real-time metrics) in Framer is a nightmare filled with iframes, external scripts, and unstable hacks.</p>
            <p><strong class="text-white">Astro + React (The new web):</strong> It is the absolute standard of the Blockchain industry. You can import `@solana/web3.js` or `ethers.js` natively. The website is no longer just "informational"; it is now the technical foundation upon which ZERA can build its official dApp without ever leaving the domain or the architecture.</p>
          </div>
        </section>
        
        <!-- Conclusion -->
        <div class="mt-16 rounded-[2rem] bg-gradient-to-br from-amber-500/20 to-orange-600/5 border border-amber-500/30 text-center relative overflow-hidden card-responsive">
          <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[radial-gradient(circle_at_50%_50%,rgba(255,136,0,0.15),transparent_60%)] pointer-events-none"></div>
          <h3 class="text-3xl font-extrabold text-white mb-6 relative">The Verdict</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-amber-100/80 mb-8 max-w-2xl mx-auto relative leading-relaxed">
            Framer is excellent for quickly validating a marketing idea. But for an <strong>infrastructure blockchain network</strong>, using a "low-code" tool projects the wrong image. Maintaining technical control, dominating code-level SEO, and paving the way for on-chain integrations requires an architecture exactly like the one we just built.
          </p>
          <a href="/zera-web/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full bg-amber-400 px-8 py-4 text-sm font-black uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-black transition hover:bg-white hover:scale-105 duration-300 relative">
            See the Web in Action
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" class="lucide lucide-arrow-right h-4 w-4"><path d="M5 12h14"/><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"/></svg>
          </a>
        </div>

      </main>
      
      <footer class="mt-24 border-t border-white/5 pt-8 text-center text-stone-500 text-sm">
        <p>Strategic Document Prepared for the ZERA Network Core Team.</p>
      </footer>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .title-responsive {
    font-size: 2.25rem;
    line-height: 2.5rem;
  }
  .container-responsive {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    padding-right: 1.25rem;
  }
  .card-responsive {
    padding: 2rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 640px) {
    .title-responsive {
      font-size: 3.75rem;
      line-height: 1;
    }
    .container-responsive {
      padding-left: 2rem;
      padding-right: 2rem;
    }
    .card-responsive {
      padding: 3rem;
    }
  }
</style>
